### Tested versions

- Reproducible in: 4.7.dev (commit 1aabcb9e9b)

### System information

N/A — affects all platforms using GDExtensions.

### Issue description

Several GDExtension API functions in `core/extension/gdextension_interface.cpp` dereference the `p_object` parameter without null checks. If an extension passes a null pointer (due to a bug or misuse), the engine crashes with a null pointer dereference.

Interestingly, some nearby functions in the same file **do** properly guard against null — notably `gdextension_object_cast_to()` at line 1403 and `gdextension_object_get_class_name()` at line 1390. This inconsistency suggests the missing checks are an oversight.

**Affected functions:**

`gdextension_object_get_instance_binding` (line 1365):
```cpp
static void *gdextension_object_get_instance_binding(GDExtensionObjectPtr p_object, ...) {
    Object *o = (Object *)p_object;
    return o->get_instance_binding(p_token, p_callbacks);  // crash if p_object is null
}
```

`gdextension_object_set_instance_binding` (line 1370):
```cpp
static void gdextension_object_set_instance_binding(GDExtensionObjectPtr p_object, ...) {
    Object *o = (Object *)p_object;
    o->set_instance_binding(p_token, p_binding, p_callbacks);  // crash if p_object is null
}
```

`gdextension_object_free_instance_binding` (line 1375):
```cpp
static void gdextension_object_free_instance_binding(GDExtensionObjectPtr p_object, ...) {
    Object *o = (Object *)p_object;
    o->free_instance_binding(p_token);  // crash if p_object is null
}
```

`gdextension_object_set_instance` (line 1380):
```cpp
static void gdextension_object_set_instance(GDExtensionObjectPtr p_object, ...) {
    Object *o = (Object *)p_object;
    ClassDB::set_object_extension_instance(o, classname, p_instance);  // crash if null
}
```

`gdextension_object_get_instance_id` (line 1412):
```cpp
static GDObjectInstanceID gdextension_object_get_instance_id(GDExtensionConstObjectPtr p_object) {
    const Object *o = (const Object *)p_object;
    return (GDObjectInstanceID)o->get_instance_id();  // crash if p_object is null
}
```

`gdextension_object_has_script_method` (line 1417):
```cpp
static GDExtensionBool gdextension_object_has_script_method(GDExtensionConstObjectPtr p_object, ...) {
    Object *o = (Object *)p_object;
    ...
    ScriptInstance *script_instance = o->get_script_instance();  // crash if null
}
```

`gdextension_object_call_script_method` (line 1428):
```cpp
static void gdextension_object_call_script_method(GDExtensionObjectPtr p_object, ...) {
    Object *o = (Object *)p_object;
    ...
    *(Variant *)r_return = o->callp(method, args, p_argument_count, error);  // crash if null
}
```

**For comparison, `gdextension_object_cast_to` does check for null (line 1403):**
```cpp
static GDExtensionObjectPtr gdextension_object_cast_to(GDExtensionConstObjectPtr p_object, ...) {
    if (!p_object) {
        return nullptr;
    }
    Object *o = (Object *)p_object;
    ...
}
```

### Steps to reproduce

This is a source-level bug. It can be triggered by any GDExtension that accidentally passes a null `Object*` to any of the above functions (e.g., after an object has been freed and the extension still holds a reference).

### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)

N/A — API contract issue visible from source analysis.
